  "strategy": "Approach and rationale\nThe core idea is to minimize the AC1 upper bound by iteratively refining a step-function representation using linear programming (LP) and coordinate descent optimization. The approach leverages harmonic analysis insights by treating sequences as weighted sums of basis functions, parameterizing complex-to-convex constraints, and balancing convexity with high-degree harmonics. The central hypothesis is that sequences achieving the lower bound must possess near-orthogonality in their FFT components paired with specific harmonic phasing.\n\nThe method excels by:\n1. Handling adaptive component decomposition\n2. Preserving sequence length through reparameterization\n3. Maintaining tight numerical tolerances against floating-point limitations\n4. Using structured initialization that incorporates the parent sequence\n5. Employing a hand-crafted coordinate optimizer that prioritizes FFT-aligned updates\n\nKey limitations include:\n- Heuristic convergence detection\n- Empirical parameter tuning\n- Potential sensitivity to initial conditions\n- Fixed parameter normalization\n\nThe solution assumes equality of representation within initialization bounds and relies on closed-form FFT coefficient summation rather than costly matrix constructions.\n\nMathematical specification\nVariables:\n- x = [x1, x2, ..., x\u2099] \u2208 \u211d\u207a\u207f (sequence values)\n- a = [a1, a2, ..., a\u2096] \u2208 \u2115\u207a\u1d4f (basis components)\n- c \u2208 [0, 1000] (component capacity)\n- \u03b3\ua734 \u2208 {0,1} (active components)\n\nObjective:\nMinimize \u03a9 = [ minX\u0338\u2098] subject to:\n\nPrimary components: a\u211b/Q\nAuxiliary harmonics: \u03c6(a) - RF\u0302(\u2193) \nFFT coherence: \u03c6_FFT(x) - variable \u03c6(\u2193)\nUtility score: fitness(x) = \u03a8(-\u222b[\u00b7]) + \u211d\u1d56\n\nConstraints:\n1. Non-negativity: \u2200i, x_i \u2265 0\n2. Normalization: \u03a3x\u2099 \u2265 0.01\n3. Length retention: track_all_components(\u00b7) = true\n4. Fidelity: \u2016x - x\u771f\u5b9e\u2016\u2081 \u2264 \u03b5\n5. Convexity: \u039b(x) \u2265 \u03b2 \u00b7 \u039b optimum\n\nImplementation procedure\n1. Initialization\n- Represent sequence as superposition of basis functions\n- Start with random blending of logarithmic and polynomial components\n- Use provided height_sequence_1 as primary initializer\n- Pad/fallback to [1,1,...,1] (n-unique)\n\n2. LP Direction:\n- Solve max\u2096 \u03a3\u03bb\u2096 subject to (f*g) coerced in L\u221e\n- Find binding strict constraints (non-zero dual variables)\n- Project sequence space using active basis\n\n3. Coordinate Optimization:\n- Golden-section search on rescaled axes (golden_ratio_r(perturb))\n- Combine energy placement with frequency domain constraints\n- Block-iterative harmonic pursuit (IPE)\n\n4. Temperature Scheduling:\n- Main iteration: cooling schedule\n- Local escape: pivot-switching\n- Global reset: if no progress, random mutation\n\n5. Accuracy Guaranteeing Checks:\n- Verify sum(len or feature) \u2265 0.01\n- Clip values: max(0, min(1000))\n- Check finite values before objective computation\n- Redundant sum calculation\n\nSearch choices and variations\n1. Initialization patterns:\n   - Primary: parent height_sequence_1\n   - Variations: sawtooth, balanced peaks, logarithmic decay\n   \n2. Update scheduling:\n   - Multi-phase: aggressive \u2192 cautious\n   - Cooling rates: exponential with max phase duration\n\n3. Dimensionality control:\n   - Start at 20 components, max 40\n   - Component ratio controlled by harmonic frequency\n\n4. Visualization helpers (debug only):\n   - Component contribution plots\n   - Local extrema detection\n\nComputation budget and robustness\n1. Memory profiling:\n   - FFT planning: next_fast_len(2n-1)\n   - Matrix construction: padded to next power of 2\n\n2. Time checks:\n   - Phase switching based on timing\n   - Timeout triggers fallback\n\n3. Stability measures:\n   - NaN/Inf checks\n   - Fallback using golden ratio sequence\n\n4. Component maintenance:\n   - Remove saturated coordinates\n   - Dynamic spacing during optimization\n\nValidation and return contract\n1. Pre-filtering:\n   - Zeros reduced via mean reassignment\n   - Finite checks\n\n2. Final validation:\n   - evaluator_sequence_check(x)\n   - Fallback: uniform sequence with normalization\n\n3. Normalization assurance:\n   - explicit_sum_enforcement(\u03be))\n   - failure coerces to normalize with fallback\n\n4. Output format:\n   - Valid non-empty list\n   - Belpartial_\u230axo\u230baising sequence verified by AC1 score\n\nThis hierarchical approach differentiates from the parent by explicit component basis selection and coordinated global-local optimization. The method is theoretically grounded in harmonic analysis yet practically optimized for execution resources.",
